# Purpose: teach Economics to convert Strategy production demand percentages into concrete city production.
# Economics general inputs: input[961]=city count, input[962]=free city count, input[965]=own military count, input[966]=enemy military count, input[974]=idle movable units, input[975]=worker count, input[976]=opened technology rate, input[980]=settlers demand, input[981]=worker demand, input[982]=explorer demand, input[983]=military demand, input[984]=money account, input[985]=account delta, input[986]=upkeep.
# City fields used: population, food income, production income, money income, frontier flag, seaside flag, and garrison strength.
# Decision meaning: produce Settlers because Strategy wants expansion and the city has food.
# Output candidates: output[0] = produce Settlers; output[1] = produce Explorer; output[2] = produce Worker; output[3] = produce Warrior; output[4] = produce Slinger; output[5] = produce Archor; output[6] = produce Spearman; output[7] = produce None.
# Correct answer: choose output[0] = produce Settlers.
# Evaluation rule: after inference, compare only those candidate outputs; the highest value is the predicted answer.
# Training target: output[0] is set to +0.900000, every other candidate output is set to -0.900000.
